   WHERE vtid='VTID-03745';"

# Located the ring: grepped vitana-v1 (community app) for 'speaking'/orb
# widget references, confirmed it loads the gateway's
# /command-hub/orb-widget.js at runtime (useOrbVoiceWidget.ts,
# orbActivate.ts, devHub.config.ts all reference it), then grepped this
# repo's copy for the CSS:
grep -n "vtorb-mic|vtorb-btn|controls" \
  services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
#   -> found .vtorb-btn-mic.vtorb-mic-live { box-shadow: ... } (line ~521)
#      and the classList.toggle('vtorb-mic-live', ...) call site (~3778)
#      that drives it (full duplex + audio playing + not muted).

grep -rn "mic-live" services/gateway/test/
#   -> only a source comment in the widget-parity test, referencing the
#      class NAME, not the box-shadow CSS. Confirmed via:
grep -rn "box-shadow|rgba\(34,197,94" services/gateway/test/
#   -> no matches. Safe to remove the CSS without touching the class-toggle
#      logic the parity test cares about.

# Fix: removed the box-shadow rule; updated the two adjacent comments
# (_injectStyles and _updateUI) that referenced/justified the ring so they
# don't describe dead behavior; bumped orb-widget.js's ?v= cache-bust param
